    IF   `the file`'s `verification needed`
    THEN 30
    ELSE 15

@ref Article 4.2.4 (src 301-303)
GIVEN `the file` IS A `A claim file`
GIVETH A DATE
`Article 4.2.4 — the last day for Tasco to pay, for` `the file` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the file`'s `date the complete and valid file was received`
    WHEN JUST d  THEN d PLUS `Article 4.2.4 — the days Tasco has to pay, for` `the file`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the payment period has not started, because no complete and valid claim file has been received`

@ref Article 4.2.4: the period runs from the receipt of a complete and valid file, and from nothing else
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the payment period has not started, because no complete and valid claim file has been received` MEANS
    REFUSE "the payment period has not started, because no complete and valid claim file has been received"

-- The same duty, as a regulative rule. THE UNIT IS DAYS, counted from the receipt of the complete
-- and valid file; the deadline is inclusive (WITHIN 15 is in time on day 15).
@ref Article 4.2.4 (src 301-303)
GIVEN `the file` IS A `A claim file`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the rules`
`Article 4.2.4 — Tasco must pay the claim` `the file` MEANS
    PARTY  `Tasco Insurance`
    MUST   `pay the claim`
    WITHIN `Article 4.2.4 — the days Tasco has to pay, for` `the file`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `Tasco Insurance`
           BECAUSE "Tasco did not pay within 15 days (30 where it had to verify the file) of receiving the complete and valid claim file"

§§§ `4.2.5 — a file Tasco cannot verify itself`

-- src:304 | Trường hợp Bảo hiểm Tasoo không đủ thẩm quyền để xác minh các yếu tố trong hồ sơ,
-- src:305 | thì hồ sơ bồi thường được coi là đầy đủ và hợp lệ sau khi có kết luận chính thức của cơ
