    WHEN JUST d  THEN d PLUS 15
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the payment period has not started, because no complete and valid claim file has been received`

@ref Article 4.2.6 (src 314-316)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the rules`
`Article 4.2.6 — Tasco must explain a refusal in writing` MEANS
    PARTY  `Tasco Insurance`
    MUST   `explain the refusal in writing`
    WITHIN 15
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `Tasco Insurance`
           BECAUSE "Tasco did not explain its refusal in writing within 15 days of receiving the complete and valid claim file"

§§§ `4.2.1 to 4.2.3, 4.2.7 to 4.2.10 — Tasco's other duties`

-- Src 318-331, not quoted. (2.8) is a permission ("có thể tạm ứng"): Tasco MAY advance part of the costs once it has
-- decided the loss is covered; nothing obliges it. (2.9) is the counterpart of Article 5.2.5.
-- The rest are duties with no date and no measurable outcome; carried, not modelled.

§§ `Article 5 — Rights and duties of the policyholder, owner and driver`

-- Src 333-346, not quoted. Rights; given effect where they matter by Articles 3.2 and 9.

§§§ `5.2.1 to 5.2.4 — reading the rules, paying, declaring, inspection`

-- Src 348-362, not quoted. (2.1) deems the policyholder to have read and understood the rules once the policy is received.
-- (2.3) and (2.4) are duties whose breach Article 14.1.2(d) penalises.

§§§ `5.2.5 — a change in the risk, within 05 days`

