-- A change in what the premium was based on must be notified within 05 days of the change. A
-- decrease lets the policyholder ask for less premium, and end the contract if refused; an
-- increase lets Tasco recompute, and end the contract if the policyholder refuses.
@ref Article 5.2.5 (src 364-367)
GIVEN `the date of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Article 5.2.5 — the last day to notify Tasco of a change in risk made on` `the date of the change` MEANS
    `the date of the change` PLUS 5

@ref Article 5.2.5 (src 364-367)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the rules`
`Article 5.2.5 — the policyholder must notify a change in risk` MEANS
    PARTY  `the policyholder`
    MUST   `notify Tasco of the change in risk`
    WITHIN 5
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the policyholder`
           BECAUSE "the policyholder did not notify Tasco within 05 days of a change in the basis of the premium"

