-- (c): written notice within 5 days of the loss, except in force majeure or an objective obstacle.
-- Article 14.1.1(b) penalises the same failure with 10%, but excuses only force majeure or an
-- assessment by Tasco within the period, NOT an objective obstacle (finding X-04).
@ref Article 5.2.7(c) (src 402-405)
GIVEN `the date of the loss` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Article 5.2.7(c) — the last day for written notice of a loss on` `the date of the loss` MEANS
    `the date of the loss` PLUS 5

@ref Article 5.2.7(c) (src 402-405)
GIVEN `the circumstances` IS A `The circumstances`
      `the conduct`       IS A `The conduct after the loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 5.2.7(c) — the duty to give written notice was met` `the circumstances` `the conduct` MEANS
        `the conduct`'s `force majeure prevented the written notice`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `objective obstacle prevented the written notice`
    OR  `sent by the last day`
    WHERE
        `sent by the last day` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the conduct`'s `written notice of the loss sent on`
            WHEN JUST d  THEN d AT MOST `Article 5.2.7(c) — the last day for written notice of a loss on` (`the circumstances`'s `date of the loss`)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

@ref Article 5.2.7(c) (src 402-405)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the rules`
`Article 5.2.7(c) — the policyholder must send written notice of the loss` MEANS
    PARTY  `the policyholder`
    MUST   `send a written notice of the loss`
    WITHIN 5
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the policyholder`
           BECAUSE "no written notice of the loss was sent within 5 days of the loss"

